      "committer": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mikekinney@Mikes-MacBook-Pro.local",
        "date": "2026-11-09T16:56:23Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(ui): fixture UX - mark/import from the browser, mesh state, struck tint\n\n#339 slice 4. A model row's context menu offers \"Use as fixture\" (bound\nto the active setup) / \"Stop using as fixture\" through the existing\nTagFixture / UntagFixture commands; a setup's Fixtures node offers\n\"Import fixture…\", which now lands mesh and marker as one undo unit\n(new ImportFixture command; it was two).\n\nEach Fixtures row shows how the gate judges the steel: \"mesh\" or\n\"box only: <reason>\" from #476's MeshError (open mesh, non-finite,\ncollapsed, over the facet cap, no facets) or a shared box. The Fixtures\npage prints the full sentence. app::fixture_view computes it, cached\nper document version.\n\nWhen the selected op has FixtureHit warnings, app::fixture_struck\njudges each fixture on its own with the post gate's per-op law\n(op_hits, which posting::fixture_problems now shares). The fixtures\nthat reproduce a warned move are tinted in the viewport (vertex class\nSTRUCK_CLASS -> gouge colour) and named in the op banner. A warned move\nthat no fixture reproduces is reported as unresolved and nothing is\ntinted for it. This is display only.\n\nRefs #339\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
