        "date": "2026-11-09T17:17:25Z"
      },
      "message": "Merge issue/339-fixture-mesh-v2 (with upstream/main 70c261ba) into issue/339-fixture-ux\n\nTakes the parent PR #476 after its merge of upstream/main (#464\nstack_span, #462 carry-machine check, #470 MCP setup/machine/fixture\ntools), so this branch is current with main too.\n\nConflict resolution:\n- crates/app/src/posting.rs: #470 split the gate walk into\n  fixture_problems (strings) over fixture_findings ->\n  Result<FixtureFindings, String> (hits as (op, warning) pairs plus an\n  unjudged list), which #476 carried with the mesh_refined *_held laws\n  inline. This branch had moved that per-op law into\n  fixture_struck::op_hits so the viewport tint and the gate share it.\n  Kept the refactor: fixture_findings calls op_hits once per op (which\n  holds #476's mesh_refined bands/rapids with steel_stack and #368's\n  tool_body::judged), Ok hits go to out.hits, Err (a body that no\n  longer fits its tool) goes to out.unjudged as \"{op}: tool T: why\" -\n  the exact string main produced. fixture_problems stays main's, so\n  the gate, the MCP get_fixture_findings tool and the struck-fixture\n  tint all read one law.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
